src/main.inset:9:5-9:13
the field `number_2` has no name in WIT
an external component's bindings are generated from WIT, which cannot keep this name
help: an external component's messages, parameters and fields are named in `snake_case`, with each word starting with a letter, such as `line_two`

src/main.inset:33:29-33:41
`Decimal` in an external component's message is not supported yet
the generated bindings cannot give the Rust code this type yet
help: carry it as a type the bindings give back exactly: a `String`, a number, `bool`, `char`, a `Vec`, an `Option`, a `Result`, a tuple, or a struct or enum of the program

src/main.inset:33:51-33:71
`HashMap<String, u32>` in an external component's message is not supported yet
the generated bindings cannot give the Rust code this type yet
help: carry it as a type the bindings give back exactly: a `String`, a number, `bool`, `char`, a `Vec`, an `Option`, a `Result`, a tuple, or a struct or enum of the program

src/main.inset:33:76-33:80
`u128` cannot cross into an external component
the WebAssembly component model has no such type
help: use an integer of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, such as `u64`

src/main.inset:35:8-35:11
an external component's functions are messages
other components reach it only through `#[message]` functions
help: write `#[message]` above the signature

src/main.inset:35:8-35:11
the message `new` takes no `self`
a message is handled by the running component
help: take `&self`, or `&mut self` to change the component's state

src/main.inset:35:8-35:11
an external component's message cannot be named `new`
the generated trait's `new` starts the component
help: give the message another name

